// Service Installed From a Suspicious Path
// Detects a new service whose binary lives in a user-writable directory or is launched through an interpreter. Services are a durable, SYSTEM-level foothold and legitimate ones almost never run out of temp.
// techniques: T1543.003   severity: high   status: stable
// validate: Atomic Red Team T1543.003
//   sc.exe create TyrianTest binPath= C:\Windows\Temp\p.exe start= auto
// source: rules/persistence/service-creation-suspicious-path.yml  (GENERATED, do not edit by hand)
Event
| where (((EventID == 7045)) and ((ServiceFileName contains @"\Temp\" or ServiceFileName contains @"\Users\Public\" or ServiceFileName contains @"\AppData\" or ServiceFileName contains @"\ProgramData\" or ServiceFileName contains @"powershell" or ServiceFileName contains @"cmd.exe /c" or ServiceFileName contains @"rundll32")))
